{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task AGENT-TF-01 is about implementing a Toolformer API-call filtering mechanism. Let me understand what's needed:\n\n1. For each call, compute: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by prediction tokens: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. Accept a call if:\n   - `parseable == true`\n   - `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return:\n   - `accepted_call_ids`: list of accepted call IDs (in original order)\n   - `diagnostics`: list of per-call objects with `call_id`, `accepted`, `normalized_gain` (in original order)\n\nThe normalized_gain should be rounded - let me think about the rounding. The schema says `\"type\": \"number\"` so it could be float. The candidate artifact says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but doesn't specify precision. Let me check the fixture data to infer.\n\nLooking at case 0:\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, tokens=5, normalized = 0.3125312\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, tokens=4, normalized = 0.09449076\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, tokens=6, normalized = 0.12425022\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, tokens=5, normalized = 0.1519078... wait 0.7595393/5 = 0.15190786\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, tokens=5, normalized = 0.041967602\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, tokens=4, normalized = 0.190983035\n\nWith threshold=0.05:\n- call0: 0.3125 \u003e= 0.05, parseable=True → accepted\n- call1: 0.0945 \u003e= 0.05, parseable=True → accepted\n- call2: 0.1243 \u003e= 0.05, parseable=True → accepted\n- call3: 0.1519 \u003e= 0.05, parseable=True → accepted\n- call4: 0.0420 \u003c 0.05, parseable=True → rejected\n- call5: 0.1910 \u003e= 0.05, parseable=True → accepted\n\nSo accepted_call_ids = [\"call0\", \"call1\", \"call2\", \"call3\", \"call5\"]\n\nThe \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I'll round to a reasonable precision. Perhaps round to 10 decimal places or use Python's default float representation. Actually I think just returning the float without excessive rounding is fine - the schema just says \"number\". Let me not add extra rounding unless specified.\n\nWait, the candidate_artifact says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" This suggests rounding. But to what precision? I'll round to, say, 10 decimal places to avoid floating point artifacts, or perhaps just use the raw computation.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, I think I should just compute and return the float value. The \"rounded\" might just mean \"properly computed\" not \"artificially truncated\". I'll round to a reasonable number of decimal places, like 10.\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    required_call_fields = {\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"}\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        # Validate fields\n        for field in required_call_fields:\n            if field not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing required field '{field}' in call\")\n        \n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        normalized_gain = round(normalized_gain, 10)\n        \n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me verify case 002 to check the parseable=False handling:\n- call4: parseable=False, so it should be rejected even though gain is positive.\n\nLet me verify: gain = 1.35899862 - 0.11897463 = 1.24002399, tokens=4, normalized = 0.31000...\nBut parseable=False → rejected. Good.\n\nNow let me format this as the required JSON output with `implementation` key containing the Python source as a string.\n\nThe output must be:\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}\n```\n\nLet me write the final implementation carefully.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Toolformer API-call filtering: retain calls whose normalized gain\\n    (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens \u003e= threshold\\n    AND whose parseable flag is True.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field 'threshold' in case\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field 'calls' in case\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    required_call_fields = {\\n        \\\"call_id\\\",\\n        \\\"loss_without_call\\\",\\n        \\\"loss_with_call\\\",\\n        \\\"prediction_tokens\\\",\\n        \\\"parseable\\\",\\n    }\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        missing = required_call_fields - set(call.keys())\\n        if missing:\\n            raise ValueError(\\n                f\\\"Call is missing required fields: {sorted(missing)}\\\"\\n            )\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(tokens, (int, float)) or tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(\\n                f\\\"prediction_tokens must be a positive number for call '{call_id}'\\\"\\n            )\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append(\\n            {\\n                \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n                \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n                \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            }\\n        )\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics,\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_016F6pnJZUJ9I7s5o9NqV784","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2470,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":49,"output_tokens":1880,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1361},"service_tier":"standard"}}